/*
 * DONKEYK - miniature Donkey Kong (arcade level 1) for the original MAKERbuino
 *           / Gamebuino Classic  (ATmega328P, 84x48 PCD8544 LCD, 3 buttons + D-pad)
 *
 * Library : Gamebuino Classic 0.5.2 (Arduino Library Manager: "Gamebuino Classic")
 * Board   : Arduino/Genuino Uno (ATmega328P @ 16 MHz) - export the *standard* HEX
 *           (NOT the "with_bootloader" one) and rename it DONKEYK.HEX
 *
 * Design notes
 *  - No dynamic memory, no big RAM arrays: all graphics live in PROGMEM.
 *  - Positions are fixed point (1/8 pixel) in int16_t; no floating point at all.
 *  - Playfield is generated from a tiny table (6 girders + Pauline's ledge),
 *    so there is no tile map in RAM.
 *  - High score: EEPROM bytes 0..2.  The Gamebuino loader mirrors EEPROM to
 *    DONKEYK.SAV when you return to the loader (C+A hold, or C on title).
 *
 * Original sprites / code, written for this project. Not affiliated with
 * Nintendo. "Donkey Kong" is a Nintendo trademark; this is a fan homage.
 * Released under LGPL-3.0-or-later to match the Gamebuino library.
 */
